{"name":"Flaming June","hex":"#eebb66","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["On fire with visible flames.","Very bright and the color of flame."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of flame"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flaming"},{"term":"june","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rush."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/june"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flaming June","blocks":[{"text":"Flaming June is a painting by Sir Frederic Leighton, produced in 1895. Painted with oil paints on a 47-by-47-inch square canvas, it depicts a sleeping woman in a sensuous version of his classicist Academic style. It is Leighton's most recognisable work, and is much reproduced in posters and other media."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flaming_June%2C_by_Frederic_Lord_Leighton_%281830-1896%29.jpg/330px-Flaming_June%2C_by_Frederic_Lord_Leighton_%281830-1896%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flaming_June"},{"title":"Flaming June (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Flaming June\" is an instrumental by American electronica musician BT. Released on June 30, 1997 through Perfecto Records as the lead single from his second studio album ESCM, it features co-production from German DJ and producer Paul van Dyk, and was remixed by British musician Chicane."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cc/BT_FlamingJune.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flaming_June_(song)"},{"title":"June","blocks":[{"text":"June is the sixth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars—the latter the most widely used calendar in the world. Its length is 30 days. June succeeds May and precedes July. This month marks the start of summer in the Northern Hemisphere and contains the summer solstice, which is the day with the most daylight hours. In the Southern Hemisphere, June is the start of winter and contains the winter solstice, the day with the fewest hours of daylight out of the year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG/330px-Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Study_for_Flaming_June_by_Frederic_Leighton.jpg/500px-Study_for_Flaming_June_by_Frederic_Leighton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Study_for_Flaming_June_by_Frederic_Leighton.jpg/500px-Study_for_Flaming_June_by_Frederic_Leighton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leighton's study for Flaming June","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStudy_for_Flaming_June_by_Frederic_Leighton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Dorothy_Dene_1880s.jpg/500px-Dorothy_Dene_1880s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Dorothy_Dene_1880s.jpg/500px-Dorothy_Dene_1880s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dorothy Dene in the 1880s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADorothy_Dene_1880s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of